       "rows": [
        "Committee"
       ]
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "start": 3.79,
     "end": 12.765,
     "text": "A Monte Carlo engine simulates thousands of price paths from the stock's own history, using two methods — block bootstrap, and GARCH.",
     "focus": [
      {
       "sel": "[data-testid=agent-spine]",
       "rows": [
        "Committee"
       ]
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "start": 12.985,
     "end": 18.585,
     "text": "It asks: how often does price hit the target first, the stop first, or neither, in time?",
     "focus": [
      {
       "sel": "[data-testid=agent-spine]",
       "rows": [
        "Committee"
       ]
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "start": 18.805,
     "end": 24.93,
     "text": "That's a no-edge baseline. It tells the committee how much edge the setup must supply to be worth taking.",
     "focus": [
      {
       "sel": "[data-testid=agent-spine]",
       "rows": [
        "Committee"
       ]
      }
     ]
